From: millia ampora <198710911+dappermint@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: skip the exchange when setting an already-signalled
 msync event

Ported for CrossOver 26.3 from dappermint/winecx commit
ef72fdb55b9274f61ba42d3c4e7a6981179bd455 (branch wine1119),
code unchanged except as noted below. A downstream msync fix, not a
WineHQ backport: WineHQ has no msync. Runs only when WINEMSYNC is set.

Adaptation: a sequentially consistent fence before the early read keeps
SetEvent a full barrier when the event is already set, as it is on
Windows; the fence does not take the cache line exclusive, which is
what the original change avoids.

SetEvent on an event that is already set changes nothing and wakes nobody, but
the unconditional exchange still takes the cache line exclusive. a thread that
signals in a loop, which is what a producer feeding a worker pool looks like,
then holds the line against every waiter trying to take the event.

read first and return when it is already set. the exchange still runs for the
0 to 1 transition, which is the only case that has to be atomic against another
signaller.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
@@ -744,6 +744,18 @@
 {
     struct event *event = get_shm( obj );
     LONG current;
+
+    /* Read before the exchange. Setting an event that is already set changes
+     * nothing and wakes nobody, but the exchange still takes the line
+     * exclusive, and a thread that signals in a loop then holds it against
+     * every waiter trying to take the event. */
+    /* Keep SetEvent a full barrier when it returns early, as on Windows. */
+    __atomic_thread_fence( __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST );
+    if (__atomic_load_n( &event->signaled, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE ))
+    {
+        if (prev_state) *prev_state = 1;
+        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
 
     if (!(current = __atomic_exchange_n( &event->signaled, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST )))
         signal_all( (void *)event, obj );
